#
# Conformance case: transaction/memory-triad-execute.
#
# The LIVE EXECUTION of the memory MCP triad as a Transaction-Logic transaction (the companion to
# transaction/trajectory-audit, which is the read-only audit). The world facts (input.nq) record a
# gmeow:ToolCall sequence — the triad's store_claim then revise_belief — anchored under a turn that
# runs logic:CommittedExecution. The native auditor groups the bound ToolCalls
# (logic:instantiatesSchema) under their logic:properPartOf anchor (which bears the
# logic:transitionFromState start state), orders them by gmeow:atTime, right-folds them into a
# logic:SerialConjunction, and runs the executional-entailment engine. Because the governing
# contract COMMITS, a successful run materializes the executed path and the per-step situation-level
# supersession — revise_belief's logic:del retiring the stored claim's support (Principle 10:
# superseded, never erased). This is exactly what the live server commits when a write tool's
# precondition obtains.
#
# The world facts seed the teleology evaluator; this input.logic.ttl carries the minimal,
# clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the projections need. The contract selects the
# Evolution facet (logic:TransactionPathEvolution) that classifies the audited transaction, and
# declares logic:CommittedExecution for fidelity with the world-facts wiring.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/transaction/memory-triad-execute/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .

ex:TransactionContract a logic:ReasoningContract ;
    logic:evolution logic:TransactionPathEvolution ;
    logic:executionMode logic:CommittedExecution .
